description:
@RuralJapan 
聖地・熊野、三重県御浜町きて、初めて見る雪は世話が焼ける。
でも、真っ白な町はいつもより、ワクワクする

Mount Yake (or Yakedake), an active volcano, looms over the Kamikochi valley, and if you hike to it's summit, you can get extraordinary views of the mountain range and valley below. We did our hike along the Shin-Nakanoyu trail, which can be accessed via car. Mt. Yake is especially great as it's one of the few mountains you can do as a day hike in the Northern Alps.  

//COME SAY HI!
Patreon (free behind the scenes content!): https://www.patreon.com/RoyandAimee
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//LINKS:
Japan Meteorological Agency (English): https://www.jma.go.jp/bosai/map.html#10/36.145/137.644/&contents=volcano&lang=en
Mt. Yake volcanic rating (Japanese): https://www.data.jma.go.jp/vois/data/tokyo/STOCK/activity_info/310.html

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

#japan #hiking #kamikochi

We have big plans for winter, and want to explore all the wonderful aspects of this season in Japan. From winter festivals and winter hikes, to snowboarding and steamy bowls of ramen. This is our first winter season with our brand new (to us) van, and we've had to make a few adjustments in order to live the winter van life. Travel with us to the snowy town of Yuzawa on our first test run, (and near disaster) and see how it all pans out!

//COME SAY HI!
Patreon (free behind the scenes content!): https://www.patreon.com/RoyandAimee
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//TRAVEL INFO: 
Echigo Yuzawa Station "Bomb onigiri" (and sake tasting) - https://www.ponshukan.com/en/yuzawa/

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

//CHAPTERS: 
00:00 Preparing our van for winter
03:18 Staying overnight in the van in -4 degrees
09:15 Yuzawa's special onigiri (and Sake!)

#japan #travel #vanlife

Japan's Northern Alps have some of the most coveted and dangerous hikes in the entire country. On this trip, we set out to hike two of these peaks — Mt. Chogatake and Mt. Jonen — on a 15.5 hour, overnight hike. More than ever before we experienced a lot of great highs and many lows, all with beautiful views of the alps around us. 

//COME SAY HI!
Patreon (free behind the scenes content!): https://www.patreon.com/RoyandAimee
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//TRAVEL INFO: 
The hike - https://thejapanalps.com/en/route/mt-jonen/route-02/
The trailhead - https://maps.app.goo.gl/kT8aeLP89eJUWFzV6

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

#japan #hiking #travel

This day hike in Japan's central alps has been one of our favourite so far! Getting off the Komagatake Ropeway at 2600m, you're immediately greeted by Senjojiki Cirque, a beautiful mountainous area. From there, you can either do a 45 minute, easy walk around the area or, like us, hike the 4 hour round-trip to Mt. Kiso-Komagatake. 

//COME SAY HI!
Patreon (free behind the scenes content!): https://www.patreon.com/RoyandAimee
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//TRAVEL INFO: 
Komagatake Ropeway: https://chuo-alps.com/lang/en/

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

#hiking #japan #travel

Rainy season in Japan from around mid June to early July is a very hot, humid and... rainy time of the year. That didn't stop us though! We took our new campervan to a free campsite in Yamanashi to try out cooking and camping in the van for the first time. Join us as we attempt to have a bbq, stay cozy despite the rain and enjoy Japan's nature.

//COME SAY HI!
Patreon (free behind the scenes content!): https://www.patreon.com/RoyandAimee
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//TRAVEL INFO: 
