Camping in Japan can be cheap! We’ve been finding some fantastic free campsites to help keep the cost of our travels low, allowing us to travel for longer. In this video we want to share with you guys what our routine is like at the end of day when all the action is over. We share with you things like how we cook, what we do with our rubbish, the facilities you can expect at a free campsite, and how we usually spend our evenings.

//COME SAY HI!
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//TRAVEL INFO:
Hanaizumi Sports Park Camping Ground -
https://goo.gl/maps/jSc6GeCkgEjuwaJ18
Van rental - https://camgo-campervan.com/

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

Camping on top of a mountain in Shiretoko, Hokkaido has been one of our favourite outdoor experiences to date. Shiretoko National Park 知床国立公園  has one of the highest densities of bears in the world, so hiking this track was a little scary but camping at the top was well worth it!
#camping #japan

//COME SAY HI!
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//TRAVEL INFO:
Mount Rausu 羅臼岳 - https://hikinginjapan.com/2008/09/24/mt-rausu/
Shiretoko National Park - https://www.env.go.jp/en/nature/nps/park/shiretoko/index.html

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

Daisetsuzan National Park in Hokkaido, Japan has been described as a hiker's paradise because of its many pristine hiking tracks through the mountains. We decided to tackle Hokkaido's tallest mountain - Mt. Asahidake, which also happens to be an active volcano. 

You can take a ropeway half way up the mountain which means its a manageable 2 and a half hour hike to the top. It's still fairly hard work though, so make sure you're feeling fit before you go (not like us haha!). 

//COME SAY HI!
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

A short day trip away from Tokyo is this amazing nature spot called Okutama 奥多摩町 where you can relax and unwind, and get an excellent feel for the countryside of Japan. Here you can go swimming, fishing, camping, have a bbq, and soak up the great outdoors. And what's best - it's easily accessible by public transport - no car required.

//COME SAY HI!
Patreon (free behind the scenes content!): https://www.patreon.com/RoyandAimee
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

Camping next to the ocean is a relaxing experience - listening to the sounds of the waves, and chirping insects as you fall asleep. In this video we share with you where and how we camped in Chiba (千葉県) and the beautiful attraction of Mt. Nokogiri (鋸山).

The Chiba region is only a 40 minute trip across Tokyo bay aboard the Tokyo-Wan ferry. It costs 900 yen per person per way - but it’s also just as easy to get to this region by taking trains.

We took local trains to the town of Tomiura (富浦) and took a bus to Cape Daibusa (大房岬) where we camped in the state forest’s campground. It was a wonderful, kid-friendly, cheap campground, with plenty of amenities that only cost ￥650 per night. 

//TRAVEL INFO:
Campground - http://taibusa-misaki.jp/mp.cgi/camp

//COME SAY HI!
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

#camping #japan #japantravel #chiba

Just two hours from Tokyo, the area around Mount Fuji, in Yamanashi prefecture, is packed with fun things to do, and of course, great views of Mount Fuji. We show you around Kawaguchiko, where you can camp, bike ride and lounge in the lakeside park, as well as the city of Yamanashi which is renowned for wineries and fruit production. 

One of the highlights of our trip was picking cherries and peaches at a local orchard. If you are planning a trip to this area, you can use public transport but hiring a car would make the trip that much more efficient and enjoyable. 

//COME SAY HI!
Patreon (free behind the scenes content!): https://www.patreon.com/RoyandAimee
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//TRAVEL INFO:
Fruit picking - http://nakagominouen.com/en/

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

Languages are weird. Have you ever wondered how a Japanese, Korean or English-speaking person might make an animal sound? In this video we show you the differences between animal sounds like a frog, monkey and pig and their pronunciations in English, Japanese and Korean. 

//COME SAY HI!
Patreon (free behind the scenes content!): https://www.patreon.com/RoyandAimee
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

We had the amazing opportunity to stay in a traditional Japanese inn (ryokan 旅館) and experience an outdoor onsen (露天風呂) in winter time with snow all around us! If you are ever visiting Japan in winter we would highly recommend this experience! We stayed in Ganiba Onsen in Akita and during our time at the ryokan we also got to experience a traditional multi-course Japanese dinner and breakfast. 

//COME SAY HI!
Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/royandaimee/

//MUSIC FROM: 
Epidemic Sound - https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/zjyf0a/

